  "problem": "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{-7n}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Recall the following special limit: \n\n$$\ne={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{n}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the given limit using the algebra of limits, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{-7n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{[{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{n}]}^{-7} \\\\  & ={[{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{n}]}^{-7} \\\\  & ={e}^{-7} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
